From fc67547e47f2b74acdd5a28dcd3a7724722a3e7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:24:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] microblaze: use the ELF maximum object-file alignment

MicroBlaze capped MAX_OFILE_ALIGNMENT at 32768 bytes, so
__attribute__ ((aligned (65536))) on a variable was an error, although
the assembler and linker handle larger alignments: a .data section with
.balign 1048576 assembles with sh_addralign 1048576 and links at a
1 MiB boundary.  Drop the override and use elfos.h's (1 << 28) bytes,
which gcc.dg/attr-aligned-3.c expects of ELF targets.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/microblaze/microblaze.h (MAX_OFILE_ALIGNMENT): Remove.
---
 gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.h | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.h b/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.h
index 9cb52a20a..8aa8d6c6a 100644
--- a/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.h
+++ b/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.h
@@ -784,9 +784,6 @@ extern int save_volatiles;
 #define GLOBAL_ASM_OP			"\t.globl\t"
 #define LCOMMON_ASM_OP			"\t.lcomm\t"
 
-#undef MAX_OFILE_ALIGNMENT
-#define MAX_OFILE_ALIGNMENT		(32768*8)
-
 #define ASM_OUTPUT_DEF(FILE,LABEL1,LABEL2)                            \
  do { fputc ( '\t', FILE);                                            \
       assemble_name (FILE, LABEL1);                                   \
